{
  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "scriptId": "log-04-logarithmic-equations-nested-logs",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Logarithmic Equations and Nested Logs",
    "description": "Solve equations containing logarithms by converting to exponential form, combining log terms, and working from the outside or inside as needed.",
    "teachingApproach": "Treat each equation as a shape-changing problem: first isolate or combine the logarithm, then convert to exponential form. Use simple equations before nested logs and related bases, and check the final value in the original log expression.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 31,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 10, Logarithms. Solve log_a f(x)=k by converting to f(x)=a^k, equal-log equations with the same base, sums and differences of logarithms, and equations that produce a simple quadratic. Teach nested logarithms from the outside inward, as in log_2[log_3(log_2 x)]. Include equations using two related bases such as log_4 x + log_2 x and source-style equations where a constant 1 is rewritten as log_10 10 before combining. Check that the final value makes every logarithm in the original equation meaningful."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's solve equations where the unknown is inside a logarithm.\n\nThe main move is simple: once one logarithm is isolated, turn it back into exponential form.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Suppose log₂(x+1)=4.\n\nConvert the log to a power:\n\nx+1=2^4=16\nso x=15.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The logarithm is only telling you the exponent. Once you convert it, the rest is an ordinary equation.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_1": {
