    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Subtracted logs become a quotient.\n\nlog₃x − log₃2 = 2\nbecomes\nlog₃(x/2)=2.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Then x/2=3^2=9, so x=18.\n\nThe quotient law often turns two logarithms into one clean equation.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
